.TH WSPANEL-INSTALL 8 "" "WSPanel" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
wspanel-install \- set up or upgrade WSPanel on this server
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B wspanel-install
.RB [ \-\-yes ]
.RI [ installer-options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Sets the server up from the installed
.B wspanel
package: PHP, databases, the web server and TLS proxy, mail, DNS, the panel
and its first administrator. Without options it asks (a guide in the
terminal); on a server that has WSPanel already it offers to upgrade with
the current settings, kept in \fI/etc/wspanel/install.flags\fR.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-yes
No questions: the options given, or the saved ones on an installed server.
.TP
.BI \-\-panel\-domain= domain
The panel's address (or \fB\-\-panel\-port=\fIport\fR for an IP address).
.TP
.BI \-\-admin\-email= email
The first administrator (the password is generated and printed).
.PP
All installer options are listed in the WSPanel documentation
(docs/instalace.md).
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
sudo wspanel-install
sudo wspanel-install \-\-yes \-\-panel\-domain=panel.example.com \e
  \-\-acme\-email=admin@example.com \-\-db=mariadb \-\-admin\-email=admin@example.com
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR wspanel-update (8),
.BR panel-agent (8)
